# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

Manages cluster node configurations that will be applied to CAST AI provisioned nodes.
If you choose to add new node configuration that will be applied to all newly provisioned nodes, you will have to mark
it as the default using `castai_node_configuration_default` resource.

## Example Usage

{{ tffile .ExampleFile }}

### GKE Hyperdisk Balanced boot disks

`gke.provisioned_iops` and `gke.provisioned_throughput` configure provisioned performance for Hyperdisk Balanced boot disks:

- They require the boot disk to be `hyperdisk-balanced`. Setting a different `disk_type` alongside either value fails during `terraform plan`; if `disk_type` is unset, provisioning fails unless the machine family's runtime-resolved disk type is `hyperdisk-balanced`.
- `hyperdisk-balanced` boots only on newer machine families (see [GCP disk types](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/disks#pdspecs)); provisioning fails for families that cannot boot from it.
- When both values are set, GCP couples them: `MAX(140, provisioned_iops/256) <= provisioned_throughput <= MIN(2400, provisioned_iops/4)`.

These settings apply to **newly provisioned nodes**: existing nodes are not reconfigured in place and pick up the new values as CAST AI replaces them through its normal consolidation and upgrade flows.

